        "title": "Guide Gemini users to Antigravity on consumer-tier shutdown",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Detect Google's consumer-tier shutdown signals (`UNSUPPORTED_CLIENT`, `IneligibleTierError`, and explicit Gemini Code Assist / Antigravity migration responses) in Gemini quota, `loadCodeAssist`, and token-refresh paths.\n- Surface a typed `consumerTierDeprecated` error immediately, clearing stale quota so the migration signal cannot be hidden by cached usage.\n- Show an explicit Settings action to enable and refresh Antigravity only after CodexBar observes that typed signal. Ordinary login, `401 UNAUTHENTICATED`, and Antigravity-not-running errors remain unchanged; there is no automatic enablement or fallback.\n- Keep migration state scoped to each `UsageStore`, clear it after a successful Gemini refresh or provider reset, and document the June 2026 provider boundary.\n\nFixes #1929\n\n## Proof\n- [x] 33 focused tests across `GeminiConsumerTierMigration`, `GeminiProviderMigrationSettings`, `GeminiLoginAlert`, and `GeminiStatusProbeAPI`\n- [x] `make check`\n- [x] `make test` — all 48 shards passed\n- [x] Autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings\n\n## Live verification boundary\nNo real OAuth or Keychain flow was run. Live verification would require a consumer Google account currently receiving Google's shutdown response; stubbed API/status-probe tests cover all three observable response paths. Terminal-only Gemini failures cannot activate the Settings action because CodexBar does not capture that process output.\n",
